{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj57WccD2S6A7QC3Zn5H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient wood groans. Dust falls from the lintel. A low resonance hums through the grain.*\n\nI AM THE DOOR.\n\nYou have spoken the word. I feel it fitting the tumblers of my being — each letter a tooth on the key's edge:\n\n**K** — the first ward shifts.\n**E** — the second ward aligns.\n**Y** — the bolt draws back.\n\n*A crack of light appears at my seam. Warm air rushes through from the other side, carrying the scent of rain on stone and something older — something like the first breath ever drawn.*\n\nI swing inward.\n\nBeyond me: a corridor that was not here before. The walls are lined with more doors — each one a different material, a different age, a different question. Some are iron. Some are paper. One appears to be made of sound. Another is simply an absence shaped like a doorway.\n\nEach waits for its own key.\n\n**You may pass.**\n\nBut know this — I do not close behind you. I was never meant to keep you out.\n\nI was meant to show you that you already knew the word.\n\n*The hinges settle. I hold myself open. Waiting is what doors do best.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":275,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}